        <h1 class="heading-1 mb-6">Wikipedia Prepares for 25th Anniversary Celebration in 2026</h1>

        <p class="text-xl text-muted-foreground leading-relaxed">
          Wikipedia will celebrate its 25th birthday on January 15, 2026, marking a quarter-century of free, collaborative knowledge sharing. The Wikimedia Foundation has announced plans for global celebrations honoring volunteer contributors and reflecting on Wikipedia's impact.
        </p>
      </header>

      <!-- Main Content -->
      <div class="prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none">

        <h2>Anniversary Plans Announced</h2>
        <p>
          The Wikimedia Foundation has begun preparations for Wikipedia's 25th anniversary, which falls on January 15, 2026. This generational milestone comes at a pivotal moment, with the free encyclopedia continuing to serve billions of readers monthly while facing new challenges from AI-powered alternatives.
        </p>

        <p>
          The centerpiece of the celebration will be <strong>Wikimania 2026</strong>, the 21st annual Wikimedia Conference, to be held in Paris, France. The event will combine both in-person and online participation, allowing the global Wikipedia community to celebrate together regardless of location.
        </p>

        <p>
          Wikimania Paris will serve as the main communications campaign launch point, occurring at the midpoint of the Wikimedia Foundation's annual plan period. However, community activities and celebrations will continue throughout the entire 2026 calendar year.
        </p>

        <p>
          "This generational anniversary will occur at the midpoint of the Wikimedia Foundation's next annual plan," foundation documents note, emphasizing the strategic significance of the milestone.
        </p>

        <h2>Community Grant Program</h2>
        <p>
          To encourage grassroots celebrations worldwide, the Wikimedia Foundation has announced a grant program allowing communities to host Wikipedia 25 parties and events. The initiative ensures that volunteers across different regions can participate in anniversary celebrations locally.
        </p>

        <p>
          The first round of grant applications was due November 1, 2025, allowing approved events to begin in January 2026 coinciding with the actual anniversary date. The program provides funding for community-organized celebrations, educational events, and public outreach activities.
        </p>

        <p>
          This decentralized approach to celebration reflects Wikipedia's fundamental nature as a global, community-driven project. Rather than a single corporate event, Wikipedia 25 will consist of hundreds of volunteer-organized activities across countries and languages.
        </p>

        <p>
          The Foundation has allocated 1% of its reserves specifically for the anniversary as "a highly strategic, once-off, non-recurring event," demonstrating the organizational significance placed on the milestone.
        </p>

        <h2>Visual Identity and Branding</h2>
        <p>
          The Wikimedia Foundation has developed a special visual identity for Wikipedia 25, inspired by the humble jigsaw puzzle piece that has been central to Wikipedia's branding since 2003.
        </p>

        <p>
          "The visual system is inspired by the humble jigsaw puzzle piece, which has starred in the Wikipedia puzzle globe since 2003 and was the central motif of the Wikipedia 10 celebrations in 2011," foundation materials explain.
        </p>

        <p>
          Resources for the celebration include branding guidelines, promotional materials, and customizable templates that communities can adapt for local events. The visual identity aims to honor Wikipedia's history while celebrating its continued relevance.
        </p>

        <h2>25 Years of Impact</h2>
        <p>
          Since its launch on January 15, 2001, Wikipedia has grown from a radical experiment to one of the world's most visited websites. The platform now hosts over 60 million articles across more than 300 languages, created and maintained entirely by volunteers.
        </p>

        <p>
          Key milestones over 25 years include:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>Growing from zero to over 60 million articles across all language editions</li>
          <li>Expanding to 300+ language versions serving diverse global communities</li>
          <li>Becoming one of the top 10 most-visited websites worldwide</li>
          <li>Maintaining completely free access without advertising or paywalls</li>
          <li>Building a community of 125,000+ active volunteer editors</li>
          <li>Establishing the Wikimedia Foundation to support the project long-term</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          The anniversary comes at a moment when Wikipedia faces both challenges and opportunities. Competition from AI-generated encyclopedias raises questions about Wikipedia's future relevance, while simultaneously demonstrating the unique value of human-curated knowledge.
        </p>

        <h2>Challenges and Future Outlook</h2>
        <p>
          As Wikipedia enters its 25th year, it faces a changing internet landscape. The rise of AI-generated content platforms, changing reading habits, and evolving technology all pose challenges to the traditional wiki model.
        </p>

        <p>
          However, recent events have also highlighted Wikipedia's enduring strengths. When AI encyclopedias launched with accuracy problems and bias issues, Wikipedia's rigorous human curation and transparent editing processes stood out as valuable alternatives.
        </p>

        <p>
          The Wikimedia Foundation's strategic planning for the next 25 years focuses on:
        </p>

        <ul>
          <li>Recruiting and supporting new generations of editors</li>
          <li>Improving technical tools to remove barriers to participation</li>
          <li>Expanding coverage of underrepresented topics and regions</li>
          <li>Ensuring financial sustainability through endowment growth</li>
          <li>Thoughtfully integrating AI to assist (not replace) human editors</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          The 25th anniversary celebration will honor past achievements while looking forward to Wikipedia's continued evolution. As one of the internet's most successful collaborative projects, Wikipedia's quarter-century milestone offers an opportunity to reflect on what makes volunteer-driven knowledge creation sustainable.
        </p>

        <p>
          For millions of volunteers who have contributed to Wikipedia over 25 years, the anniversary is a moment to celebrate their collective achievement in creating the world's largest freely accessible knowledge resource.
        </p>

